---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SubpageHeader from '../components/SubpageHeader.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy — DROOCKED.ORIGINS"
  description="Privacy policy for DROOCKED.ORIGINS — hosting, analytics consent, cookies, retention, and your rights."
>
  <SubpageHeader title="PRIVACY" />

  <article class="page-section privacy">
    <p class="privacy__updated">Last updated: 14 November 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Controller and contact</h2>
    <p>
      This website, <strong>droocked.origins</strong>, is a private documentation
      project about 3D printing. The controller responsible for the processing of
      personal data on this website is the operator of droocked.origins. You can
      reach the controller for any privacy question or request at <a href="mailto:contact@droocked.com">contact@droocked.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="privacy__note">
      A full legal notice (Impressum) with a postal address is not published in
      this release. Until it is added, please use the contact email above for all
      legal and privacy requests.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Scope and principles</h2>
    <p>
      This website has no user accounts, no comments, and no newsletter. We aim to
      collect as little personal data as possible. The only optional processing
      that goes beyond the technical delivery of the site is Google Analytics 4,
      and it runs only after you give consent.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Hosting and server log data</h2>
    <p>
      The website is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, a service provided by
      GitHub, Inc. (part of Microsoft). When you open a page, GitHub processes
      technical request data in order to deliver the site and keep it secure. This
      may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>your IP address;</li>
      <li>the requested URL and the referring page;</li>
      <li>the date and time of the request;</li>
      <li>browser, operating system, and user-agent information;</li>
      <li>the response status and the amount of data transferred.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data is used to serve the website, detect abuse, and maintain
      availability and security. We do not have direct access to GitHub's raw
      server logs. GitHub processes this data under its own terms and privacy
      policy.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Google Analytics 4 (only with consent)</h2>
    <p>
      This website is built with <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> only when the
      production build defines the measurement ID <code>G-SZ67XVNMM4</code> in the
      <code>PUBLIC_GA_ID</code> build variable. Local development and preview
      builds do not include analytics at all. The GA4 library is included using the
      standard <code>gtag.js</code> snippet, without a Google Tag Manager container,
      and it processes analytics data only after you give consent. GA4 is provided
      by Google Ireland Limited for users in the European Economic Area, the United
      Kingdom, and Switzerland, and by Google LLC for other users.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every page is a normal full page load, so page views are measured directly by
      GA4. If you accept analytics, GA4 may collect:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the pages you view and the time you spend on them;</li>
      <li>approximate location derived from your IP address (GA4 does not store the full IP address);</li>
      <li>device, browser, operating system, screen size, and language;</li>
      <li>the referring source, including UTM parameters in links;</li>
      <li>
        interaction events: <code>affiliate_click</code> when a product storefront
        link is clicked, <code>social_click</code> when a social icon is clicked,
        <code>contact_click</code> when an email link is clicked, and
        <code>outbound_click</code> when another external link that opens in a new
        tab is clicked. These events record the destination URL and, for product
        links, the product and storefront identifiers — not your name, email
        address, or the contents of any message.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      All four <strong>Consent Mode v2</strong> signals —
      <code>analytics_storage</code>, <code>ad_storage</code>,
      <code>ad_user_data</code>, and <code>ad_personalization</code> — are denied
      by default before any measurement is configured. No analytics cookies are set
      and no user-level analytics profile is created until you accept. Google may
      still receive cookieless consent-state signals that do not identify you. We do
      not enable Google Signals, ads personalization, or advertising products on
      this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you accepted on an earlier visit, the stored choice is read before GA4 is
      configured, so analytics storage is granted again without showing the banner.
      You can withdraw your consent at any time with the <strong>cookie settings</strong> control at the end of this page or in the
      footer. Declining also removes existing GA cookies from this browser.
      Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing that happened before
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses the following storage. Only the consent entry is required for
      the site to remember your choice; the analytics cookies are set only after you
      accept.
    </p>
    <div class="legal-table-wrap" tabindex="0">
      <table class="legal-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Name</th>
            <th scope="col">Type</th>
            <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
            <th scope="col">Lifetime</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>droocked-consent</code></td>
            <td>localStorage</td>
            <td>Stores whether you accepted or declined analytics, so the banner does not reappear on every visit.</td>
            <td>Until you clear it or change your choice</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>_ga</code></td>
            <td>Cookie</td>
            <td>Distinguishes users for aggregate analytics. Set by Google Analytics only after consent.</td>
            <td>Up to 2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>_ga_*</code></td>
            <td>Cookie</td>
            <td>Maintains session state for the GA4 property. Set by Google Analytics only after consent.</td>
            <td>Up to 2 years</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      You can delete cookies and local storage at any time in your browser
      settings. Blocking the consent entry means the site will ask again on your
      next visit; blocking analytics cookies after consent stops measurement but
      does not change your stored choice.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Legal bases</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics:</strong> your consent under Article 6(1)(a) GDPR and, in
        Germany, Section 25(1) of the Telecommunications Digital Services Data
        Protection Act (TDDDG) for storing and reading information on your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting and server logs:</strong> our legitimate interest under
        Article 6(1)(f) GDPR in delivering the website securely, reliably, and
        without abuse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email contact:</strong> Article 6(1)(b) GDPR where your message
        relates to a contract or a pre-contractual request, otherwise Article
        6(1)(f) GDPR in answering your inquiry.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent choice:</strong> stored in your browser until you change it
        or clear your browser storage.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics:</strong> the GA4 data retention period is
        configured inside the GA4 property (Admin → Data settings → Data
        retention), not in this website's code. It is set to
        <strong>14 months</strong>, the longest event-level retention period GA4
        currently offers. Aggregated reports may be kept longer without directly
        identifying you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs:</strong> retained by GitHub for the limited period
        needed to operate and secure the service, in line with GitHub's own
        retention practices.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email:</strong> kept only as long as needed to handle your inquiry,
        unless a legal retention obligation applies.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Recipients and processors</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC</strong> — analytics processor
        for Google Analytics 4, only after consent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GitHub, Inc. (Microsoft)</strong> — hosting provider for GitHub
        Pages and technical delivery of the site.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data. Data is shared with these providers only as
      needed for the purposes above, and further disclosure happens only where we
      are legally required to do so.
    </p>

    <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Google and GitHub are based in the United States, so processing may involve a
      transfer of personal data outside the European Economic Area. Where required,
      such transfers are safeguarded by the European Commission's Standard
      Contractual Clauses and, where the recipient is certified, by the EU-US Data
      Privacy Framework. You can ask for more information about the safeguards at <a href="mailto:contact@droocked.com">contact@droocked.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectify, erase, or restrict the
      processing of your personal data, the right to data portability, and the
      right to object to processing based on legitimate interests. Where
      processing is based on consent, you can withdraw that consent at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, write to <a href="mailto:contact@droocked.com">contact@droocked.com</a>. You also have
      the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority,
      in particular in the country of your habitual residence, your place of work,
      or the place of the alleged infringement.
    </p>
    <p>
      This website does not use automated decision-making or profiling that
      produces legal effects.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Affiliate links and external services</h2>
    <p>
      Some outbound links on this site are or will be <strong>affiliate
      links</strong>, marked with an <strong>AFFILIATE</strong> badge. If you click
      an affiliate link and make a purchase, we may receive a commission at no extra
      cost to you. Product links that are not yet available are shown as <strong>LINK PENDING</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Affiliate links lead to third-party shops and networks. Those providers may
      set their own cookies and process your data under their own privacy policies;
      this policy does not cover them. The same applies to social links to
      Instagram, TikTok, and YouTube, and to any other external website. Please
      check the privacy policy of the destination before sharing data there.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated when the site, its services, or the legal
      requirements change. The date at the top of this page shows the current
      version.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For any question about this privacy policy or the processing of your personal
      data, contact <a href="mailto:contact@droocked.com">contact@droocked.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="privacy-actions">
      <button class="privacy-consent-button" type="button" data-consent-open>
        cookie settings
      </button>
    </p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
